WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to our enable weekend operations for merchant-fulfilled orders training.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Offers in the Amazon store come with a customer delivery promise.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000
This promise gives customers a date range in which they can expect an order to arrive.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.667
Customers like to receive their orders as soon as possible, so it's important to promise them the

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.000
shortest delivery time possible.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.600
The customer delivery promise is composed of handling time, transit time, and a small buffer in

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.000
case of the unexpected

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.889
like weather.

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:37.000
Today, we'll show you how to offer a better customer delivery promise by enabling weekend operations.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.000
You may notice that non-business days make the handling time longer in the customer delivery promise.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Weekends and holidays are automatically counted as non-business days in the customer delivery promise.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
So, if your handling time is normally two days and someone purchases your product on a Monday, you'll

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
be expected to ship by Wednesday.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.400
But if someone purchases your product on Friday, two days that make up the weekend will be added

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.000
to your handling time, and you'll be expected to ship on Tuesday.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Depending on the customer's needs, that can be a long time for them to wait.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
But if you're able to ship products on the weekend, you can make your listings more appealing to

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
those customers by enabling weekend operations.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.750
From the Seller central home page, select the gear icon in the upper right to open the settings

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.000
menu and then select shipping settings.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Once you're on the shipping settings menu, select the general shipping settings tab.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.625
Then scroll down to order fulfillment settings.

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:38.000
Select edit to the right to adjust these settings.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.045
Scroll down to weekend Operations settings or select it from the menu on the left to edit your settings

00:01:44.045 --> 00:01:45.000
for weekend operations.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.263
Here, you can choose to have your packages picked up by shipping providers on either Saturday, Sunday,

00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:52.000
or both.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.833
If you enabled shipping settings automation or SSA on your shipping templates to automatically calculate

00:01:57.833 --> 00:01:59.000
your delivery promise,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:05.545
you'll also need to enable weekend operations for SSA-enabled products in the shipping region automation

00:02:05.545 --> 00:02:08.000
section, which can be found below.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.105
For more information on SSA, search for shipping settings automation in Seller University or on

00:02:15.105 --> 00:02:17.000
Seller Central's help page.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.120
Once you've chosen your desired settings, don't forget to save them using the button in the upper

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.000
right or your settings selections will be lost.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Now you know how to enable weekend operations for your merchant fulfilled orders.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.444
With this setting enabled, your customer delivery promise can improve, making your products more

00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:38.000
appealing to potential buyers,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.000
especially those shopping at the end of the week.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Finally, remember that enabling weekend operations means more than just working on the weekends.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
It sets the expectation that you'll ship packages on the weekend too.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.885
So if you don't have a shipping provider that picks up packages on Saturday, don't set Saturday

00:02:55.885 --> 00:02:59.000
as a pickup day in your general shipping settings.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.000
This concludes our enable weekend operations for merchant fulfilled orders training.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
